.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt USERMOD 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm usermod
.Nd change a user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl mov
.Op Fl c Ar comment
.Op Fl d Ar home-dir
.Op Fl e Ar expiry
.Op Fl G Ar group Ns Op , Ns Ar group ...
.Op Fl g Ar gid | name
.Op Fl L Ar class
.Op Fl l Ar new-login
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Op Fl s Ar shell
.Op Fl u Ar uid
.Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility changes
.Ar user Ns 's
entry in the account database, in the shape of the
.Nx
and
.Ox
command.
It is
.Xr pw 8
under another name.
Only what is given changes.
It must be run by the superuser.
.Pp
The options are as in
.Xr useradd 8 ,
and:
.Bl -tag -width "-l new-login"
.It Fl G Ar group Ns Op , Ns Ar group ...
The supplementary groups: the user is made a member of exactly these,
and removed from any others.
.It Fl l Ar new-login
The new login name.
Group memberships follow it; the user's own group keeps its name.
.It Fl m
Move the home directory to the one
.Fl d
gives.
.It Fl o
Allow a user ID already in use.
.It Fl u Ar uid
The new user ID.
Files the user owns are not changed.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As
.Xr pw 8 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr useradd 8 ,
.Xr userdel 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Nx 1.5
and
.Ox 2.7 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
